  "interpretation": "In the TB-A06 identity-only reference-transfer context, the single precise identity lock produced the same mean identity_fidelity score as the repeated-lock control (4.75 versus 4.75, delta +0.00). Aesthetic quality improved by +0.25, technical cleanliness improved by +0.50, and semantic compliance was unchanged. The overall mean increased from 4.6875 to 4.8750 (+0.1875). This run therefore shows no observed identity-fidelity loss from using the single precise lock, but the result is classified inconclusive because no non-inferiority or equivalence margin was predeclared and the small sample cannot establish that the two identity-lock strategies are equivalent.",
